# Built binaries.
#
# `make build` writes into bin/ rather than the repo root, because katra
# dogfoods itself: ./katra is the *store directory* this project keeps its own
# log in, so `go build -o katra` would be writing over a directory.
#
# The two bare-name rules are kept for anyone who builds to the root by hand.
# `/katra` would also match the data directory, so it is re-included
# immediately — only the binary file stays ignored.
/katra
/katra-mcp
!/katra/
# A build run *inside* the data directory drops the binary at katra/katra.
/katra/katra
/bin/
/dist/

# Go build/test artifacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# The static site, when built locally for a look
/site/

# Local scratch / working files
/tmp/
/scratch/
/.scratch/
*.local
*.local.*

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Python build cache (branding/build.py)
__pycache__/
